# Accepted vulnerability advisories for `pnpm run audit:supply-chain` and the
# matching CI scan in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# Both scans read this file, so an entry here suppresses the finding locally and
# in CI alike. Add one only with a maintainer's reason for why the advisory is
# unreachable and a time-bounded follow-up, per docs/supply-chain-security.md.
# One advisory ID per line, e.g.:
#
#   CVE-0000-00000  # unreachable: <reason>; revisit by <date>

# image-size 2.0.2 (dev-only, reached through the Docusaurus docs build, which
# only reads images committed to this repository): DoS via crafted image
# buffers. No source-backed fix: the advisories list no patched version, and
# the 2.0.3/2.0.4 releases on npm have no matching tag or commit upstream, so
# they are not adopted under the quarantine policy. Revisit by 2026-10-17 or
# when a tagged release lands.
CVE-2025-71329  # unreachable: docs-build only, repository-authored images; revisit by 2026-10-17
CVE-2025-71330  # unreachable: docs-build only, repository-authored images; revisit by 2026-10-17
